//@ compile-fail
//@ error-contains: `assert` takes 1 argument, but 0 were given
//@ error-contains: `assert_eq` takes 2 arguments, but 3 were given
//@ error-contains: `assert_throws` takes 1 argument, but 2 were given
//
// The parser accepts any number of arguments to the assert intrinsics; the counts are
// enforced by the checker because they used to be enforced nowhere. `assert()` compiled
// to a silent no-op — an assertion that cannot fire, sitting in a test, looking like
// coverage.

fn f() throws str -> i64 { throw "x" }

fn main() {
    assert();
    assert_eq(1, 1, 1);
    assert_throws(f(), f());
}
